The Star Schema ⭐
Fact Table: Sales
Dimension Tables: Customers, Products, Stores, Exchange_Rates, Calendar

### Primary Keys (PKs)

These uniquely identify each record in their respective tables:
Customers → CustomerKey
Products → ProductKey
Stores → StoreKey
Exchange_Rates → ExchangedKey 
Calendar → Date

### Foreign Keys (FKs)

These are located in the Sales1 (fact table) and link to dimensions:
CustomerKey → references Customers.CustomerKey
ProductKey → references Products.ProductKey
StoreKey → references Stores.StoreKey
ExchangedKey → references Exchange_Rates.ExchangedKey
Order Date (or Delivery Date depending on active relationship) → references Calendar.Date

### Cardinalities (Relationships)

All relationships follow a 1-to-Many (1:*) structure:
Customers1 (1) → Sales1 (*)
One customer can have multiple sales
Products1 (1) → Sales1 (*)
One product can appear in multiple sales
Stores1 (1) → Sales1 (*)
One store can generate multiple sales
Exchange_Rates1 (1) → Sales1 (*)
One exchange rate entry can apply to multiple sales

The data model follows a star schema design, with the Sales table as the central fact table connected to multiple dimension 
tables through one-to-many relationships. Primary keys in dimension tables are linked to corresponding foreign keys in the fact
table, ensuring referential integrity andenabling efficient slicing of data across customer, product, store, time, and currency 
dimensions.
